#text(size: 16pt, weight: "bold")[Note:] The next chapter is "*References*," which is automatically generated by Typst from the `references.bib` file. Also, note that there is a difference between "References" and "Bibliography." The list of "References" strictly only contains the list of articles, papers, and content you have cited (i.e., referenced) in the report. Whereas Bibliography is a list that contains the list of articles, papers, and content you have cited in the report plus the list of articles, papers, and content you have read in order to gain knowledge from. We recommend using only the list of "References."
